  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.4.11: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.11\n- No functional changes in this package; see the core package notes\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.11+\n\nv0.4.10: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.10\n- No functional changes in this package; see the core package notes for the local-simulator capacity and execution changes\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.10+\n\nv0.4.9: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.9\n- Codebase-wide Fantomas formatting; no functional changes intended\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.9+\n\nv0.4.8: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.8 (core struct-union binary change — recompile)\n- fsharp-refactor code clean-up: ordinal string comparisons, use-bindings for disposables, narrower exception catches. No functional changes intended\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.8+\n\nv0.4.7: AWS SDK v4\n- UPDATED: AWS SDK for .NET to v4 (AWSSDK.Braket 4.0.*, AWSSDK.S3 4.0.*). No API surface changes in this plugin; the SDK usage (CreateQuantumTask/GetQuantumTask/S3 GetObject) is unaffected by v4's nullable-property and collection-initialization changes\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.7+\n\nv0.4.6: Wide-device result support + correctness fixes\n- NEW: ExecuteToState returns tiered results — dense state vector ≤ 20 qubits, sparse state 21-31, QuantumState.MeasurementHistogram beyond (NO width limit: at most `shots` entries regardless of qubit count) — Rigetti Ankaa (~84q) and other wide gate devices are now usable end to end\n- NEW: BraketBackend.ExecuteToHistogramAsync — raw measurement histogram (bitstring → count) at any width\n- FIXED: 21+-qubit results no longer crash with an unhandled exception (previous cap mismatch: accepted 24, state vector limit 20)\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.6+\n\nv0.4.3: Initial public release of the AWS Braket plugin\n- Submit gate circuits to Braket QPUs (IonQ, Rigetti, IQM, OQC, Infleqtion) and simulators (SV1/DM1/TN1) via OpenQASM 3.0\n- Submit QuEra Aquila neutral-atom analog programs via the Braket AHS format\n- Isolates the AWS SDK dependency so the core FSharp.Azure.Quantum package stays AWS-free\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.3+",
